x86_64-windows  cxx1 emits Held's implicit default constructor, ??0Held@@QEAA@XZ, and cl does not - it inlines the one call and emits no symbol for it. The same difference as the Itanium half of this case's .nonames: cxx1 emits every member function it is given, as an ordinary global - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol", is where that rule is written down. Every other name in the object agrees.
